WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.173 --> 00:00:03.580
(upbeat music)

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:05.381
- [Narrator] Pinball,
always an arcade favorite,

00:00:05.381 --> 00:00:08.937
but if you grew up in New York
City between 1940 and 1976,

00:00:08.937 --> 00:00:12.187
playing pinball meant breaking the law.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.767
In 1933, Congressman Fiorello
LaGuardia was elected

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.049
Mayor of New York City.

00:00:20.049 --> 00:00:22.181
One of the first items on
his agenda was to crack down

00:00:22.181 --> 00:00:23.535
on the mafia.

00:00:23.535 --> 00:00:25.999
He honed in on mob-owned slot machines

00:00:25.999 --> 00:00:28.117
and surprisingly, pinball machines.

00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:30.091
He succeeded in getting pinball declared

00:00:30.091 --> 00:00:31.528
an illegal game of change.

00:00:31.528 --> 00:00:34.151
And in 1940, the city banned the game.

00:00:34.151 --> 00:00:35.397
- I'm gonna stop it.

00:00:35.397 --> 00:00:37.439
- [Narrator] This, of course,
drove pinball machines

00:00:37.439 --> 00:00:40.874
underground to seedy parlors
and even seedier strip clubs.

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:43.303
But public disdain for
pinball wasn't as high

00:00:43.303 --> 00:00:44.791
as it was for slot machines,

00:00:44.791 --> 00:00:46.924
which made it hard for the
mayor to gain public support

00:00:46.924 --> 00:00:50.601
for his raids on these newly
illegal pinball establishments,

00:00:50.601 --> 00:00:52.576
that was until 1941.

00:00:52.576 --> 00:00:54.433
After Pearl Harbor, the
government established

00:00:54.433 --> 00:00:56.304
the salvage for victory campaign,

00:00:56.304 --> 00:00:58.720
which called on Americans
to turn in scrap metal

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.471
to be used for the war effort.

00:01:00.471 --> 00:01:03.131
Enter Mayor LaGuardia,
who took this opportunity

00:01:03.131 --> 00:01:06.171
to seize and destroy more
than 3,000 pinball machines,

00:01:06.171 --> 00:01:09.788
all in the name of helping
the military, of course.

00:01:09.788 --> 00:01:12.266
Thirty years went past before New
York City declared pinball

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:16.183
a game of skill, not
chance, and legalized it.

